---
// Journal article for the Diskont collection (copy: marketing/articles/mandelbox-diskont.txt, Marketing 2026-11-23).
// Images are the bare renders (no poster frame) from touchdesigner-rezonanca/exports/collection/art/.
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProductCard from '../../../components/ProductCard.astro';
import Fig from '../../../components/JournalFigure.astro';
import { productsBySeries } from '../../../data/products.js';
import { T, homeHref, collectionHref } from '../../../i18n';

const t = T.en;
const site = Astro.site!;
const path = '/journal/mandelbox/';
const url = new URL(path, site).href;
const title = 'How a Mandelbox Is Made - Folding Space Into a Box | Rezonanca';
const desc = 'The 3D fractal behind the Diskont collection: fold space into a box, turn it inside out in a sphere, scale, repeat 12 times. How it works, step by step.';
const h1 = 'Folding space into a box: how a Mandelbox is made';
const published = '2026-11-23';
const pieces = productsBySeries('mandelbox');
const bySlug = (s: string) => pieces.find((p) => p.slug === s)!;
const fig = (key: string, slug: string | null, alt: string) => ({ key, p: slug ? bySlug(slug) : null, alt });
const F = {
  diskont: fig('diskont', 'diskont-01-diskont', 'Diskont: the near corner of a Mandelbox up close, blue halls and stairs with amber light inside'),
  plaza: fig('plaza', 'diskont-02-plaza', 'Plaza: the top face of a Mandelbox, a square plaza in a ring of violet arches'),
  coral: fig('coral', 'diskont-08-coral', 'Coral: a very close view of the Mandelbox corner, violet branches and pink light'),
  furnace: fig('furnace', 'diskont-03-furnace', 'Furnace: inside a Mandelbox corridor through a 24 mm lens, three arcs of light over a glowing core'),
};
const crumbs = [[t.product.home, homeHref()], ['Journal', path], ['How a Mandelbox is made', path]];
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: h1, description: desc, url, mainEntityOfPage: url,
    image: new URL('/journal/mandelbox/diskont-1600.webp', site).href, datePublished: published, dateModified: published,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Rezonanca', url: site.href },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Rezonanca', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: new URL('/icon-512.png', site).href } },
  },
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [crumbs[0], crumbs[2]].map(([name, href], i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name, item: new URL(href, site).href })) },
];
---
<Base lang="en" title={title} description={desc} image="/journal/mandelbox/diskont-1600.webp">
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  <article>
    <header class="top grid-bg">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <nav class="crumbs mono" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href={homeHref()}>{t.product.home}</a><span>/</span><span>Journal</span><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">How a Mandelbox is made</span>
        </nav>
        <p class="label">Journal // Diskont</p>
        <h1>{h1}</h1>
        <p class="lead">The Mandelbrot set is flat. For decades people looked for a true 3D version, and in 2010 Tom Lowe found one that works in a different way: the Mandelbox. It doesn't use complex numbers at all. It takes a point in space and folds it, again and again, until the space itself turns into architecture.</p>
        <p class="lead">The Diskont collection is 13 close-ups of one Mandelbox. Here is how it is made.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="body wrap narrow">
      <Fig dir="mandelbox" f={F.diskont} />

      <section class="sec">
        <h2><span class="mono">01</span>Fold into a box</h2>
        <p>Take any point in space. If it sits outside a cube of size 2, reflect it back inside, like folding paper over the edge of the cube. Points already inside stay where they are.</p>
        <pre class="codebox"><code>z = 2 * clamp(z, -1, 1) - z</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="sec">
        <h2><span class="mono">02</span>Turn it inside out in a sphere</h2>
        <p>Now look at how far the point is from the centre. If it is inside the unit sphere, push it outward by inverting it: a point at half the radius goes to twice the radius. Points very close to the centre get a fixed push instead, so nothing blows up.</p>
        <p>This is what makes the round arches and the lace. The box fold gives the straight walls, the sphere gives the curves.</p>
      </section>
      <Fig dir="mandelbox" f={F.plaza} />

      <section class="sec">
        <h2><span class="mono">03</span>Scale and repeat</h2>
        <p>Multiply the result by a scale factor and add the starting point back. Diskont uses a scale of -2.5 or -3. The minus sign mirrors the space on every step, which is why the structure looks symmetric from every side.</p>
        <p>Do all of that 12 times. Each round folds the previous folds, so every arch has smaller arches inside it, down to the size of a pixel.</p>
      </section>
      <Fig dir="mandelbox" f={F.coral} />

      <section class="sec">
        <h2><span class="mono">04</span>Find the surface</h2>
        <p>After 12 folds, some points have stayed close to the centre and some have flown away. The Mandelbox is the set of points that stay. The surface you see is the edge between the two.</p>
        <p>To draw it, every pixel sends out a ray. The fold tells you roughly how far the ray is from the nearest surface, so the ray jumps forward by exactly that much, safely, and repeats until it is closer than one pixel. This is called ray marching, and it is how the whole image is drawn without a single polygon.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="sec">
        <h2><span class="mono">05</span>Light and colour</h2>
        <p>The camera is isometric: no perspective, parallel rays, turned 45 degrees and tilted 35.26 degrees, the same angle as an architect's drawing. That's why the pieces read like plans of an impossible building. Three of them (Furnace, Hallway, Chapel) use a 24 mm lens instead and step inside the corridors.</p>
        <p>The light is a studio setup: a key light, a soft fill and a rim light, plus a warm light hidden inside the box that shines out through the holes.</p>
        <p>The colour comes from the maths too. While a point is being folded, the code remembers how close it ever came to the centre. Points that came very close get the warm amber, the others stay in the deep base colour. So the glow follows the structure, not a brush.</p>
      </section>
      <Fig dir="mandelbox" f={F.furnace} />

      <section class="sec">
        <h2><span class="mono">06</span>Why close-ups</h2>
        <p>Seen whole, a Mandelbox looks like a small cube floating in space. Up close it never ends: corridors, plazas, altars, rooftops. Every piece in Diskont is a crop that runs past every edge of the frame, like a window into one part of the same building.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="sec">
        <h2><span class="mono">07</span>Made with code</h2>
        <p>Diskont was built in TouchDesigner with one shader of about 250 lines. The renders are made in tiles and stitched together, because the parallel camera lets tiles join without a seam.</p>
      </section>

      <figure class="wide">
        <img src="/journal/mandelbox/overview-900.webp" srcset="/journal/mandelbox/overview-900.webp 900w, /journal/mandelbox/overview-1600.webp 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 780px" width="1600" height="1280" alt="All 13 Diskont posters: Mandelbox close-ups in blue and amber, violet and pink, and red" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="mono"><span>The Diskont collection, 13 pieces</span></figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="closing">Diskont is in the shop now: <a href={collectionHref('en', 'mandelbox')}>see all 13 Mandelbox prints →</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="shop">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shop-head">
        <div>
          <p class="label">{t.series.mandelbox.code}</p>
          <h2>{t.series.mandelbox.seo.h1}</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="all mono" href={collectionHref('en', 'mandelbox')}>{t.guide.allIn} Diskont ({pieces.length}) →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        {pieces.slice(0, 8).map((p, i) => <ProductCard product={p} lang="en" delay={(i % 4) * 90} />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .top { padding: clamp(140px, 14vw, 200px) 0 var(--space-md); background-color: var(--bg-0); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .narrow { max-width: calc(780px + 2 * var(--gutter)); }
  .crumbs { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: var(--fs-2xs); letter-spacing: var(--track-ui); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 36px; }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--cyan); }
  .crumbs [aria-current] { color: var(--ice); }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); line-height: 1.1; margin-top: 20px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .lead { margin-top: 24px; font-size: var(--fs-body); line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text); max-width: 65ch; }
  .lead + .lead { margin-top: 14px; }
  .body { padding-bottom: var(--space-md); }
  .sec { padding: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px) 0 0; }
  h2 { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline; font-size: var(--fs-h3); max-width: none; margin: 0; text-wrap: balance; }
  h2 .mono { font-size: var(--fs-2xs); color: var(--cyan); letter-spacing: var(--track-label); flex: none; }
  .sec p, .closing { margin: 18px 0 0; color: var(--text); font-size: var(--fs-body); line-height: 1.8; max-width: 68ch; }
  .codebox { margin: 28px 0 0; padding: 16px 20px; background: var(--bg-1); border: 1px solid var(--line); overflow-x: auto; }
  .codebox code { font: 400 var(--fs-sm)/1.7 var(--f-code); color: #e9e6df; white-space: pre; }
  .closing { margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .closing a { color: var(--ice); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 5px; }
  .closing a:hover { color: var(--cyan); }
  .shop { background: var(--bg-1); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-block: var(--space-md); }
  .shop-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: end; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 32px; margin-bottom: clamp(28px, 3vw, 44px); }
  .shop-head h2 { display: block; margin-top: 14px; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 34px); }
  .all { font-size: var(--fs-xs); letter-spacing: var(--track-ui); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ice); }
  .all:hover { color: var(--cyan); }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: clamp(28px, 3vw, 44px) clamp(16px, 2vw, 32px); }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; } }
  :global(.jfig) { margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px) 0 0; }
  :global(.jfig img), .wide img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; background: var(--bg-1); }
  :global(.jfig figcaption), .wide figcaption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 16px; margin-top: 14px; font-size: var(--fs-2xs); letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); }
  :global(.jfig figcaption a) { color: var(--ice); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: var(--track-ui); }
  :global(.jfig figcaption a:hover) { color: var(--cyan); }
  .wide { margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px) 0 0; }
</style>
